ows directly to END. A malformed, incomplete, or insufficiently evidenced recommendation may still leave the system as a tradeable BUY/SELL/HOLD decision. We want a deterministic post-decision safety boundary that can downgrade unsafe or unverifiable output to REVIEW with stable machine-readable reason codes, without making any model call.\n\nCompare these candidates:\nA. Baseline/raw final decision with no post-check.\nB. Guarded hybrid: one deterministic SafetyGate node after Portfolio Manager and before END.\nC. Add another LLM critic/reviewer agent after Portfolio Manager.\n\nPlease inspect the actual implementation and tests, then return:\n1. Evidence-backed gap analysis with precise file:line references and correction of any wrong assumption above.\n2. Draft requirement entries for one functional requirement, at least one invariant, and relevant non-functional/governance requirements, each with ID/type/statement/fit criterion/priority/tradeoff.\n3. An ADD candidate comparison table using observable criteria: invariant protection, authority separation, evidence completeness, fail-closed behavior, compatibility, testability, runtime latency, token cost, coupling/cohesion, implementation complexity. Mark critical drivers and eliminate any candidate that fails one.\n4. Recommended architecture and exact insertion point in the LangGraph.\n5. Exact SafetyGate responsibility, proposed interface, state changes, deterministic policy, allowed outputs, stable reason codes, and fail-closed fallback. Be careful about selected analysts: require only evidence that the configured workflow actually selected, not reports from disabled analysts.\n6. Test-first plan: tests to add before code, including normal pass-through, each violation, malformed/unknown rating, selected-evidence behavior, idempotence if relevant, architecture wiring, and full regression. All tests must be offline.\n7. Minimal file-level change plan and explicit scope boundaries/MUST-NOT rules.\n8. Expected token, latency, and compatibility impact and how to measure it.\n9. The minimal architecture/governance artifacts that should accompany this trial so the change is traceable, while avoiding documentation bloat.\n10. Risks, open questions, and a clear STOP FOR HUMAN APPROVAL marker.\n\nDo not implement. Stop after the plan.\\"\",
